{"title":"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c87ffb791483f5eb7b7cfe68f44c77bbfdf728dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is given such way that for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/c/4bc8b95ed989d460e11db0001adc1cd930dfebd8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6g(1 + (1/y)) + 12g(y + 1) = \\log_{10} y\\]\" width=\"284\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/6/3163a0b9f87495d61d5150d0335e08fda06ce124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(9) + g(26) + g(126) + g(401) = \\frac {m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"284\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime integers, computer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two 5-digit numbers are called \"responsible\" if they are:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edbb8a7911bd204919b88bd7faa9d7f65978a760.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp;\\text {i. In form of abcde and fghij such that fghij = 2(abcde)}\\\\ &amp;\\text {ii. all ten digits, a through j are all distinct.}\\\\ &amp;\\text {iii.} a + b + c + d + e + f + g + h + i + j = 45\\end{align*}\" width=\"404\" height=\"66\" />\n</p><p>If two \"responsible\" numbers are small as possible, what is the sum of the three middle digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d9921af26983187bc46a607f550f7b79c194c08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {abcde}$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and last two digits on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f84eff23900da5abc01044cfec9595b9615fdf0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text {fghij}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />? That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/4/fe4923be8e8f87c666ca04d544cb2f0b530e5994.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b + c + d + i + j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"128\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A triangle is called <i>Heronian</i> if its perimeter equals the area of the triangle. <i>Heronian</i> triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84614f20f337820ee6b9dd1d2f27e74e3ca80dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> has sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/5/b25e378d39e6f217be57124b07e4c4317b5ffc62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29,6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. If the distance from its incenter to the circumcenter is exprssed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/8/258c814401850924eb51cccc193df5f2d2a921fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {\\sqrt b}{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"25\" height=\"41\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is not divisible by squares of any prime, find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Eight boxes are numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. The number of ways you can put 16 identical balls into the boxes such that none of them is empty is expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/180d3d9b52be4cb06b5ae611b2ff79016eccc184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom {a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/41185aca6192c6b20a7be3554266c834d85725c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\le \\frac{a}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"34\" />. What is the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/180d3d9b52be4cb06b5ae611b2ff79016eccc184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom {a}{b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"33\" height=\"53\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/f/5df6a591474ffd81edd37d8d9f52f6f476caa531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />? \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are three rooms in Phil's Motel. One room for one person, one room for three people, and another one room for four people. Let's say Peter and his seven friends came to the Phil's Motel. How many ways are there to house Peter and his seven friends in these rooms?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Larry and his two friends toss a die four times. From all possible outcomes, the probability that outcome has at least one occurrence of 2 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/4/2846db355f537b5e50a721c7a83fe61e1f4a9084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/8/30859f119368408770ed213e9b150d451a7104c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|p - q|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/0418562731679936038fd69468e148b0ff25a698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle RST$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />, X is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/24807a6aa89451ed04d24261b78e73a5f3bd371e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {RT}$\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" />, dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/a/d9a5aec1381690120aabbda47af16d2b40652ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$RX:XT = 1:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"132\" height=\"13\" />. Y is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90efb1556d29a3462d61c3be3ed1dab7446c9c0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {ST}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72225c27fb8281792988f11c25d339354c46308f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SY:YT = 2:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"126\" height=\"13\" />. V is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/7/7b70bac4fa2b7b1cb8521205b6c7b735de14c2c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {XY}$\" width=\"31\" height=\"15\" />, dividing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541ca1d7683dc94ba5ab7ac6d6e9caa8cd0a7623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XV:VY = 1:2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"132\" height=\"13\" />. It is found that ray VT intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/a/0ba02d15c228d304616b0f8109d71178eeb77820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {RS}$\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" /> at Z. Find\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f202b459db5e98680a59341703338000668f0dc5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[128 (\\frac {TV}{VZ} + \\frac {RZ}{ZS})\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/b/4abfadd378cdd0a2b00d60bcba8f4ab24f12641c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y, \\in \\mathbb {Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" /> and that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82e73eaa497f83e8848e755827fc7bb7a3a9f7d2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x + \\sqrt y = \\sqrt {22 + \\sqrt {384}}.\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f17a2aa06cb1a262cbd837f798b6dad77e8d75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {x}{y} = \\frac {p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"50\" height=\"36\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/6/7b66443107b6eeb21448ea5a14d8d74c8ffd6ca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p,q) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"18\" />, then what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856ee48ce76ddbd106a05384c2ea2c28e3b76c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On a circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/a/fda38f45a64bbd4451aedeeb4584e01d91239172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"18\" />, two points, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are on a circle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> is outside the circle but in ray XY. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/b/cebdb99e0bee7b2fa0d3eca3d4c7832872c51906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {XY} = 33.6, \\overline {YZ} = 39.2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"184\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06335f14e4767d884a17c0f943fcf205d624ff8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {\\zeta X} = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"22\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/87704689930afbcd41c1651a47d0097f28e7c963.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {\\zeta Z} = \\frac {j}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"59\" height=\"37\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> are relatively prime integers, and such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a588c8e04424f56079bdf62dc2c418554156736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {j + k}{j - k} = \\frac {o}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"80\" height=\"41\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/a/04a14d6e2339ed5650d1a45680fff1bdfe80535d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o + p.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b77d2a17924869942c7ec4284fdf143af613881.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}(\\frac {1}{r})(\\frac {1}{s})(\\frac {1}{t}) &amp;= \\frac {3}{391} \\\\ r + \\frac {1}{s} &amp;= \\frac {35}{46} \\\\ s + \\frac {1}{t} &amp;= \\frac {1064}{23} \\\\ t + \\frac {1}{r} &amp;= \\frac {529}{102}.\\end{align*}\" width=\"142\" height=\"167\" />\n</p><p>Then what is the smallest integer that is divisible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c889d12451d321614e219737373586e45b71a141.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs$\" width=\"16\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/c/18cdf14ccf1f6fb2a2a998eed350787cc89e111b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12t$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />? \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> number of ways to represent 10000000 as product of three factors and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> number of ways to represent 11390625 as product of three factors.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa565804a19d0c6ccdb46b03227e189a372c29e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z - Z| = p^q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856ee48ce76ddbd106a05384c2ea2c28e3b76c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 11 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2722d7c4bd448964c25c6e26465b1c0434597c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 101^4 + 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />. Find the sum of digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the reciprocal of sum of real roots of the following equation can be written in form of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/6/9d66543320b3b9a1ba69d64d56643a4f5052add5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {r}{s}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132889c972033d1295c05778030c4819dfd56f94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317440729faba2b233a3547c42e9baccad52b82d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r + s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/1/12182d19910dd166f3cfd3e8eda2cc9b69f86907.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000x^6 - 1900x^5 - 1400x^4 - 190x^3 - 130x^2 - 38x - 30 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"465\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> contains complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f99e2ec1a007aa0f2b2e18a35641a62e0c3ec078.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta_0,\\zeta_1,\\zeta_2...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/8/bb8b75f1bf549ac1e114beb6aaf30b251e566fd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 0,1,2,3.....$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/2/762976ebb910157823e89c62aebbff7be29870c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" /> is defined this way:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165fc225272b554269d3eca67bb825b058cad1a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta_{n + 1} = (\\frac {\\zeta_n - i}{\\zeta_n + i})^{- 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"141\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fadfdba0718c2242330aff38da1b229951e086e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta_0 = i + \\frac{1}{121}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"38\" /> and 2008th number of the set is in form of (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe0b3c32b3838c0b06fd8e2dca022007728b5a1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />), find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/b/b9b62914e21bf2aff66deb0a46807cecd21080af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\log_2 1] + [\\log_2 2] + [\\log_2 3] + ....[\\log_2 64]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"306\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Let the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/d/8edfccca1806b08cd91daaf1f8c8fc6b43531ace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\log_2 1] + [\\log_2 2] + [\\log_2 3] + ....[\\log_2 52]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"306\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a42a8b725c200085e5253db2d2fbf8dab898a8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta$\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />. Find the absolute value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693bb9b34fcf30d2010c6ce8ec1510a116999061.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\delta - \\alpha$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_5_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"Mock AIME 5 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018100344\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.055 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 443/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14464/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6638:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018100344 and revision id 179047. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}